From 3fe46c0b01e4a4e47ef8dddee36c2f12d2e76d57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 18:20:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] kubernetes: add opt-in "text-output" parameter

Wire text-output mode into the Kubernetes protocol. Adds the boolean
"text-output" parameter (default false); when enabled, the remote bytes
received on the STDOUT and STDERR channels (merged, as the exec session
runs with a TTY) are teed, verbatim, to an outbound STDOUT pipe stream in
addition to the graphical display. Gated behind "disable-copy".

Part of: enable native CLI client (issue #3).

Signed-off-by: Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte@gmail.com>
---
 src/protocols/kubernetes/io.c         |  3 +++
 src/protocols/kubernetes/kubernetes.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 src/protocols/kubernetes/settings.c   | 15 +++++++++++++++
 src/protocols/kubernetes/settings.h   |  9 +++++++++
 4 files changed, 41 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/protocols/kubernetes/io.c b/src/protocols/kubernetes/io.c
index d00e24aa..c167920e 100644
--- a/src/protocols/kubernetes/io.c
+++ b/src/protocols/kubernetes/io.c
@@ -42,6 +42,9 @@ void guac_kubernetes_receive_data(guac_client* client,
         /* Write STDOUT / STDERR directly to terminal as output */
         case GUAC_KUBERNETES_CHANNEL_STDOUT:
         case GUAC_KUBERNETES_CHANNEL_STDERR:
+            /* Tee the raw remote byte stream to the text-output pipe, if
+             * enabled. Has no effect unless text-output mode opened the pipe. */
